lojbab weighs in (informally), for what it's worth.

OK.  Maybe I am figuring out what this is about.  Or maybe not.  If this=20
"Crash Course" is on the wiki, then politeness to all the rest of us=20
readers would necessitate someone actually putting a link to it (which=20
should be included in ALL messages about the topic, since not everyone=20
reads every message).

So I've never seen this "crash course".  And I don't have the time or=20
the interest to try to find it.  But there seems to be enough=20
information to offer some guidelines.

1.  Both "The Wave Lessons" and the "Crash Course" seem to be distinct=20
and unitary items, just as is "CLL". It seems to me that any such=20
unitary items should be well-defined, and isolated.  One way is to=20
remove them completely from the normal Lojban web pages to something=20
separate, and then include a single point of entry link that is used to=20
get from the Lojban web pages to a home page for the unitary project.

2.  If the unitary project is implemented on the same wiki as the Lojban=20
web pages (as seems to be the case here), there should be a single index=20
page that lists and links to all of the component pages making up the=20
project, and maybe a separate index to any pages that comment on, or=20
make reference to, the component pages.  The project home page would=20
link to this.

3.  If the project makes use of any experimental or non-standard=20
language features, there should be maintained a list of those features=20
in one place, either on the project home page, or on the index page, or=20
on some other single page where people can look and see and thus easily=20
evaluate whether they wish to make use of the material.  It is not=20
necessary to mark each non standard use, so long as there is only the=20
single entry point into the materials, and the list of non-standard=20
features is easily found from that single entry point.

The standard language is defined by the baseline materials and any=20
changes formally approved by byfy (which hopefully will maintain a=20
single page linking to all approved changes that are not included in the=20
baseline documentation).

